    "taxSlabs": {
      "title": "GST Council Statutory Rate Slabs & Product Classifications",
      "html": "<p>Primary tax slabs established by the GST Council across India:</p><div class=\"overflow-x-auto my-6\"><table class=\"w-full text-sm text-left border-collapse border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700\"><thead><tr><th class=\"p-3 bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white\">Rate Slab</th><th class=\"p-3 bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white\">Intra-State Split</th><th class=\"p-3 bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white\">Typical Eligible Goods & Services</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class=\"p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 font-semibold\">5% Rate</td><td class=\"p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-bold\">CGST 2.5% + SGST 2.5%</td><td class=\"p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300\">Packaged food, medicines, domestic LPG, transport services (cab/train), footwear below ₹1,000.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 font-semibold\">12% Rate</td><td class=\"p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 font-bold\">CGST 6.0% + SGST 6.0%</td><td class=\"p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300\">Processed foods, fruit juices, computers, diagnostic kits, business class air tickets.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 font-semibold\">18% Standard Rate</td><td class=\"p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400 font-bold\">CGST 9.0% + SGST 9.0%</td><td class=\"p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300\">IT software & consulting, banking services, consumer electronics, restaurants, branded garments.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 font-semibold\">28% Luxury Rate</td><td class=\"p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-rose-600 dark:text-rose-400 font-bold\">CGST 14.0% + SGST 14.0%</td><td class=\"p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300\">Automobiles, air conditioners, tobacco products, cement, online gaming (plus compensation cess).</td></tr></tbody></table></div>"
    },
    "workedExample": {
      "title": "Worked GST Transaction Scenarios",
      "html": "<div class=\"space-y-6\"><div class=\"p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 bg-slate-50/50 dark:bg-slate-800/30\"><h4 class=\"text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2\">Scenario A: Intra-State B2B IT Consulting Invoice (18% GST Exclusive)</h4><p class=\"text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-3\">A Bangalore software company bills a Karnataka client ₹1,00,000 net. Intra-state supply triggers CGST 9% (₹9,000) and SGST 9% (₹9,000). Total GST is ₹18,000, creating an invoice total of ₹1,18,000. The client claims ₹18,000 as Input Tax Credit against their outward tax liability.</p></div><div class=\"p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 bg-slate-50/50 dark:bg-slate-800/30\"><h4 class=\"text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2\">Scenario B: Retail Store Purchase (18% GST Inclusive Reverse Extraction)</h4><p class=\"text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-3\">A customer purchases a smartphone at an electronics showroom for ₹23,600 inclusive of 18% GST. Net value of the phone: ₹23,600 ÷ 1.18 = ₹20,000. Embedded GST: ₹23,600 - ₹20,000 = ₹3,600 (₹1,800 CGST + ₹1,800 SGST).</p></div><div class=\"p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 bg-slate-50/50 dark:bg-slate-800/30\"><h4 class=\"text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-2\">Scenario C: Inter-State Commercial Machinery Supply (28% IGST)</h4><p class=\"text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-3\">A manufacturer in Gujarat ships manufacturing equipment valued at ₹5,00,000 to a buyer in Maharashtra. Because goods cross state borders, 100% IGST applies at 28%: ₹5,00,000 × 28% = ₹1,40,000 IGST. Total invoice: ₹6,40,000.</p></div></div>"
    },
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What is the mandatory threshold for GST registration in India?",
        "answer": "For businesses dealing exclusively in goods, the GST registration threshold is ₹40 Lakhs of annual turnover (₹20 Lakhs in special category states). For service providers, the mandatory threshold is ₹20 Lakhs (₹10 Lakhs in special category states). Any inter-state seller must register regardless of turnover."
      },
      {
        "question": "What is the difference between CGST, SGST, and IGST?",
        "answer": "CGST (Central GST) and SGST (State GST) are levied together in equal halves on intra-state supplies within the same state. IGST (Integrated GST) is levied as a single unified tax on inter-state supplies crossing state borders or imported into India, and is collected by the Central Government."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do you calculate GST from an inclusive retail MRP?",
        "answer": "To calculate the GST amount embedded inside a retail MRP, divide the MRP by (1 + GST rate) to determine the net price, then subtract the net price from the MRP. Shortcut formula: GST Amount = MRP × Rate ÷ (100 + Rate)."
      },
      {
        "question": "What is Input Tax Credit (ITC) under GST?",
        "answer": "Input Tax Credit (ITC) allows a registered business to reduce the tax it has already paid on inputs, raw materials, or business services from the output tax it owes on sales, preventing the cascading 'tax-on-tax' effect."
      },
      {
        "question": "What is the GST Composition Scheme?",
        "answer": "The Composition Scheme is a simplified GST scheme for small businesses with turnover up to ₹1.5 Crore (₹75 Lakhs for special states). Eligible businesses pay a fixed flat turnover tax (1% for manufacturers/traders, 5% for restaurants, 6% for service providers) without claiming ITC."
      },
      {
        "question": "What is an e-Way Bill and when is it required?",
        "answer": "An e-Way Bill is an electronic document generated on the GST portal for the movement of goods in a vehicle if the consignment value exceeds ₹50,000 (both for inter-state and intra-state shipments)."
      }
    ],
